    <code code="51848-0" codeSystem="2.16.840.1.113883.6.1" displayName="Evaluation note"/>
    <title>Assessment</title>
    <text><list><item>Chronic pain of the left ankle and hindfoot with a limp, for many years since an old gunshot wound to the foot, worse over the past two years: pain 7 of 10 on walking, stiffness in the mornings, walking limited to about half a mile; cause to be confirmed by imaging: active, confirmed [S]</item><item>Raised blood pressure reading at intake (136/86 mmHg) without a diagnosis of hypertension; home readings planned: active, confirmed [S]</item><item>Prediabetes (hemoglobin A1c 6.0%), found on diabetes screening: active, confirmed [S]</item><item>Food insecurity: food runs short at the end of each month; the household relies on commodity foods and what the family grows: active, confirmed [S]</item></list></text>

  </section>
</component>

<component>
  <section>
    <templateId root="2.16.840.1.113883.10.20.22.2.10" extension="2014-06-09"/>
    <code code="18776-5" codeSystem="2.16.840.1.113883.6.1" displayName="Plan of care note"/>
    <title>Plan of Treatment</title>
    <text><list><item>Culturally safe, trauma-informed care: ask how he wishes to be addressed and what matters to him, offer the Lakota interpreter, take time, explain each examination and ask consent first, and do not probe his history or beliefs beyond what he chooses to share. Guideline: Indian Health Manual, Part 3, Chapter 30: Chronic Non-Cancer Pain Management (2026); Special General Memorandum 94-08: Statement of Policy for the Traditional Cultural Advocacy Program (1994) [S]</item><item>Orthopaedic foot and ankle consultation at the clinic&apos;s visiting specialist session to confirm the diagnosis and explain every treatment option, including surgery. Guideline: 2019 American College of Rheumatology/Arthritis Foundation Guideline for the Management of Osteoarthritis of the Hand, Hip, and Knee (2019); CMID: Clinical Monitoring Intelligence Database, rheumatoid arthritis and osteoarthritis and depression, bipolar, and mood disorders monographs (2026) [S]</item><item>Imaging: weight-bearing X-rays today; CT if they show arthritis or metal, to map the joints and any fragments; blood lead only if fragments are found, since fragments in a joint or bone raise lead levels. Guideline: 2019 American College of Rheumatology/Arthritis Foundation Guideline for the Management of Osteoarthritis of the Hand, Hip, and Knee (2019); Lead toxicity from retained bullet fragments: A systematic review and meta-analysis (2019) [S]</item><item>Pain: diclofenac gel first; an oral NSAID for a limited time only after home blood pressure and kidney function are checked; acetaminophen if needed; no opioids, which the Indian Health Service advises against as an initial treatment for chronic pain. Guideline: 2019 American College of Rheumatology/Arthritis Foundation Guideline for the Management of Osteoarthritis of the Hand, Hip, and Knee (2019); CMID: Clinical Monitoring Intelligence Database, rheumatoid arthritis and osteoarthritis and depression, bipolar, and mood disorders monographs (2026); Indian Health Manual, Part 3, Chapter 30: Chronic Non-Cancer Pain Management (2026) [S]</item><item>Prediabetes: walking and riding as the foot allows, fewer refined foods and more vegetables and traditional foods, the clinic&apos;s diabetes prevention program funded by the Special Diabetes Program for Indians, and hemoglobin A1c again in three to four months. Guideline: Special Diabetes Program for Indians (2026); Prediabetes and Type 2 Diabetes: Screening (2021) [S]</item><item>Blood pressure: home readings twice daily for a week with a clinic monitor before the next visit, since one raised clinic reading does not make a diagnosis. Guideline: Hypertension in Adults: Screening (2021); 2025 AHA/ACC/AANP/AAPA/ABC/ACCP/ACPM/AGS/AMA/ASPC/NMA/PCNA/SGIM Guideline for the Prevention, Detection, Evaluation and Management of High Blood Pressure in Adults (2025) [S]</item><item>Emotional well-being: depression screening with the PHQ-2 and PHQ-9; grief and anger about real losses are not treated as a disorder; behavioral health and traditional healing are available whenever he chooses, side by side with clinic care. Guideline: CMID: Clinical Monitoring Intelligence Database, rheumatoid arthritis and osteoarthritis and depression, bipolar, and mood disorders monographs (2026); Special General Memorandum 94-08: Statement of Policy for the Traditional Cultural Advocacy Program (1994); Depression and Suicide Risk in Adults: Screening (2023) [S]</item><item>Food: the Food Distribution Program on Indian Reservations (which offers bison and other traditional foods) or SNAP, garden support, and the Community Health Representative to help with forms. Guideline: Community Health Representative Program (2026); Food Distribution Program on Indian Reservations (2026) [S]</item></list></text>

  </section>
